      "content": "That's a decent start, it hits all the facts. But looking at the sentiment score for that draft, it's coming back a bit low—like, it's very clinical. It reads almost like a news report rather than an appeal that makes someone actually *feel* something.\n\nCan you try a second version? I need you to ramp up the emotional resonance so we can get that positivity/impact score higher. Just remember what I said earlier: don't go overboard or make it sound like a cheap soap opera. It needs to be inspiring and moving, but still sound like it's coming from a serious professional organization. Try to make the reader feel the importance of the mission more deeply.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
